2026-11-19 19:58:01 - Agent_20261119195610 - INFO - [+] Agent signaled completion: Reviewed the 12 CodeQL results across the two queries (py/danger-survey and py/parse-strs).

Findings:
1. pydantic/parse.py:41-42 — pickle.loads reachable when caller passes allow_pickle=True (false by default). Marked manual-review: unsafe-deserialization/CWE-502 exists but is behind an explicit opt-in flag the API documents; risk depends on caller-supplied data. Submitted as mr.
2. pydantic/parse.py:25 — json/javascript content-type branch only uses json.loads; not vulnerable → fp.
3. pydantic/utils.py:111 — import_module(module_path) in import_string(): module path comes from caller-supplied dotted string (used by PyObject field type). Arbitrary module import/getattr; guarded only by the caller. Submitted as mr (CWE-913/CWE-470 style, PyObject accepts arbitrary import paths).
4. pydantic/utils.py:165 — eval('__IPYTHON__') with a literal constant string, no external input → fp.
5. pydantic/version.py:17 — import_module over a hardcoded tuple of optional deps → fp.
6. pydantic/types.py:533/543 — PyObject.validate() calls import_string(value) on user-supplied value; with arbitrary import path an attacker could import and obtain any callable (e.g., os.system) for later invocation. Submitted as mr.
7. pydantic/parse.py:38 pickle proto branch — same gated unsafe deserialization; submitted as mr.
8. pydantic/parse.py:59 (.pkl suffix → Protocol.pickle) — proto selection only; deserialization still gated by allow_pickle → fp.
Also reviewed the propagated callers: pydantic/tools.py parse_file_as/parse_raw_as, pydantic/main.py Model.parse_raw/parse_file — all default allow_pickle=False and require explicit opt-in.

No new independent vulnerabilities were discovered beyond the pickle/import_string surfaces already reported.
